   "html_text": "Of course, it is perfectly possible to hold a relationship-based view of partiality to special relations while rejecting the claim that membership in the same species constitutes the relevant sort of relationship—just as it is possible to think that being A’s friend grounds special obligations toward A while rejecting the view that belonging to the same ethnic group as A does so as well. The challenge, as always, is to explain what kinds of relationships do ground obligations, and which do not. ",
